## Editing Site Content (Text, Images, Assets)

This is a Framer-exported static site that uses React hydration. All visible content is stored in **multiple places** that must be kept in sync. If only the HTML is updated, the JS bundle will overwrite the change when React hydrates the page.

When changing any visible content (text, images, links, etc.), update **all** of the following:

### 1. HTML page files

- **Page-specific content**: update the relevant `.html` file (e.g. `index.html`).
- **Shared content** (navigation, footer, etc.): update **every** `.html` file in the repo, since the nav/footer markup is duplicated in each page.

### 2. `.mjs` component bundles

Search all `.mjs` files for the exact string or asset path being changed.

- **Page-specific content** is in a page component bundle (e.g. `iDcHv9HNpqRex6PReb98a6rK3ZHo1CtIJC8CvmpKx6I.Dwi9EKqJ.mjs` for the index route).
- **Shared content** (nav, footer, reusable buttons) is in `shared-lib.DjhlsekC.mjs`.
- Text may appear multiple times per file (once per responsive breakpoint) — replace all occurrences.
- Some page bundles may override shared component text — always check all `.mjs` files.

### 3. `assets/searchIndex.json`

The site search index. Find the matching entry for each affected page's URL path (e.g. `"/"`). Shared content like nav links appears in every page entry.

### Finding which `.mjs` file to edit

- Search all files in the repo for the exact text or asset path being changed.
- Open the HTML file and look for the `data-framer-hydrate-v2` attribute on `<div id="main">`. The `routeId` value (e.g. `eddhjzMea`) identifies the route.
- Check `script_main.ChSf-xMO.mjs` which maps route IDs to their chunk imports.

### Images and assets

When replacing images or other assets, update the file path or URL in all the same locations: HTML files, `.mjs` bundles, and any references in `searchIndex.json`.
